1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:09,760
THE CHARACTERS, RACES,
AND LOCATIONS ARE FICTIONAL.

2
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:12,880
THE HISTORY OF MINORITY STRUGGLES IS REAL.

3
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:07,000
I say we just attack them head-on.
Catch them off guard.

4
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,320
-Let's go.
-No way.

5
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,960
We go in there, we're dead men.

6
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:13,680
You're right. We're outnumbered.

7
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,080
So we need to use our heads

8
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,560
to minimize our losses.

9
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,880
The order came down.

10
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,760
Crush the Kase

11
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,800
before the monsoon hits.

12
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:34,000
You call it. Any village you want.

13
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:37,000
We'll raze them to the ground.

14
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,560
It's not that simple.

15
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:42,080
The key target village

16
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:45,120
has never been breached by any squad.

17
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:48,120
You mean Naka Village.

18
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,400
Exactly.

19
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:53,320
If we take down Naka, the other villages

20
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,600
won't be a problem.

21
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:57,160
Still I believe

22
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:03,440
no matter how skilled
Colonel Layee and the Kase warriors are…

23
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:09,120
they stand no chance against us.

24
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:13,360
We the Savins
outclass them on every front.

25
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:22,880
They're holding captives.

26
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:44,120
<i>The Savins hold prisoners</i>
<i>to do their dirty work.</i>

27
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:48,160
The men are used as pack mules
for rations, meds, and munitions

28
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,040
while the women

29
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:52,520
are kept to satisfy their lust.

30
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,960
We have to save them.

31
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:58,120
Don't bother. These prisoners
have nothing to do with our mission.

32
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,280
How can you say that?

33
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,400
We're here to crush them,

34
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,160
-not save prisoners
-We should help them.

35
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,160
I disagree.

36
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,920
We stick to the plan. No exceptions.

37
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,680
Rescuing prisoners
won't ruin the plan that much.

38
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:14,360
I'm in command here!

39
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:17,080
Everyone follows my orders.

40
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:22,280
Anyone who disobeys will be punished.

41
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:26,160
Alright, follow Yapo's orders only.

42
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:30,280
It's time. Get ready.

43
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,840
Listen up. We don't have much time.

44
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:37,680
Hit them hard and pull out fast.

45
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:07,680
Retreat now!

46
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,280
Hunt them down and kill them all!

47
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:58,120
Mintada? Where's Mintada?

48
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:02,960
How should I know? We were running
together. He may have gotten lost.

49
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:07,160
Now what? The plan was for
everyone to gather right here.

50
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,080
Damn it!

51
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:13,080
If he's not here, that's his problem.
We're out of time. Move!

52
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:16,600
Wait, hold on. Mindada's coming.
He knows the meetup spot.

53
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,440
Move now!

54
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,640
-Go.
-Move.

55
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:24,480
Where the hell were you?

56
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,680
I can't leave the captives.

57
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,600
You dare disobey my order?

58
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,280
I'll take the punishment.

59
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,560
We have to go now, Yapo.
The Savins are coming for us.

60
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,200
Damn it!

61
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:37,960
Let's move.

62
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:55,240
We're on the right track.
They went this way.

63
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:57,240
Let's go. Move fast.

64
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,320
How did it go?

65
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:08,840
Everything's fine,

66
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:11,400
except someone went rogue.

67
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:17,440
We'll deal with that later.
Now take cover. Mongjunai.

68
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,880
Move!

69
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,320
Go, go.

70
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,520
Where did they go?

71
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,559
Hey.

72
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,120
Hey!

73
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:23,680
Hey!

74
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,560
Hey, don't die on me.

75
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:30,240
Hang in there.

76
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:35,480
Mintada, watch out!

77
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,320
Mintada!

78
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:59,720
Siprai. Siprai. That's enough. He's dead.

79
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:02,320
-That's enough!
-Mintada! Mintada!

80
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,240
Grab all their weapons.

81
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:08,760
Yes, Sir.

82
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,040
I've got you.

83
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,800
One, two, heave.

84
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:19,360
Let's move.

85
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,040
Move.

86
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:35,920
<i>Kase! Kase!</i>

87
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,280
Kase!

88
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:46,200
Everyone, disperse and get some rest.

89
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:47,960
Yes, Sir!

90
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:52,320
Mintada, how are you feeling, Son?

91
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:53,680
Except Mintada!

92
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:58,560
Colonel Layee, can't you see
Mintada is injured?

93
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:01,040
Insubordination demands punishment,

94
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:03,440
regardless of his injuries.

95
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,320
Fine.

96
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:11,000
I'll take the punishment I deserve.

97
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,280
Good.

98
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,640
Everyone else gets out.

99
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,040
Layee.

100
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:20,520
I said everyone else gets out!

101
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,160
If you're going to punish Mintada
for disobeying orders,

102
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:25,560
punish me too.

103
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:28,040
Consider me complicit.

104
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,360
Fine.

105
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,200
Have it your way.

106
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:42,680
In battle, disobeying orders

107
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,360
is a grave crime.

108
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:49,120
One man's lack of discipline
can ruin the entire mission

109
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,920
and endanger us all.

110
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,560
I must punish you.

111
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:55,840
Gun Tossing!

112
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:07,640
-Colonel Layee, Mindada is badly wounded.
-No, Siprai.

113
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:12,440
This isn't your fight.
Don't take the hit for me.

114
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:15,880
No. We never leave each other behind.

115
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,880
Comply!

116
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,560
Mintada.

117
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,720
Mintada.

118
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:29,720
Colonel Layee.

119
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:32,440
-Please have mercy on him Colonel Layee.
-Auntie.

120
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,520
Comply!

121
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:40,360
Colonel, Mintada is severely hurt.

122
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,520
Postpone the punishment.

123
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,520
No.

124
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:45,360
Orders are orders.

125
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,280
I was shot far worse,

126
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:51,680
surrounded by Savin troops
in the jungle for a month.

127
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:53,440
But I survived.

128
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,840
And Mindada will too.

129
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:02,400
-Can you make it?
-I can.

130
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,960
Kase warriors never die!

131
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:19,360
Kase warriors never die!

132
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:23,760
Kase warriors never die!

133
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,600
Kase warriors never die!

134
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:30,760
Kase warriors never die!

135
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,360
Kase warriors never die!

136
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:39,040
Kase warriors never die!

137
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,920
Kase warriors never die!

138
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,920
Kase warriors never die!

139
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,920
Kase warriors never die!

140
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:54,520
Kase warriors never die!

141
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:58,320
Kase warriors never die!

142
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:02,640
Kase warriors never die!

143
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,480
Kase warriors never die!

144
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:54,880
It's weird.

145
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:57,680
Why did the rain come early this year?

146
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,920
Earlier the better.

147
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:04,400
We can rest easy
knowing the Savins won't raid us.

148
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:08,000
True. Rain stops the fighting.

149
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:11,640
The Savins won't attack till it clears up.

150
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:14,080
I wish it'd rain forever.

151
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,080
No more fighting,

152
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:21,160
no more blood, no more loss.

153
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:24,240
No chance. Keep dreaming.

154
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:28,880
Not while the Savins
seek to take our Kase land.

155
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:06,120
Your village! Hey! Siprai!

156
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,840
Dad! Mom!

157
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,640
Dad!

158
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,960
Mom! Dad!

159
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:17,320
-Come here!
-No! Let me go!

160
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,240
Hold her!

161
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,160
Rena!

162
00:16:57,920 --> 00:16:59,480
Mintada, let me go!

163
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,560
-Mintada. Let go!
-Ouch! Stop!

164
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,319
Stop!

165
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:06,560
I'm not Mintada. I'm Khengla!

166
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:08,800
Don't go in, Siprai. It's dangerous.

167
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,119
I have to go!

168
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:12,520
-Stop! Siprai!
-Let me go!

169
00:17:12,599 --> 00:17:14,160
-Get off me!
-Siprai!

170
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:18,400
-Siprai!
-Siprai! Stop!

171
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,599
Stop!

172
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:26,240
Mintada, why are you stopping me?!
I have to get in.

173
00:17:26,319 --> 00:17:29,800
No way. We're not letting you go.

174
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,280
Going in there means death.

175
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:35,280
But my parents and sibling
are in there! I have to go!

176
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:38,680
-Siprai!
-Siprai!

177
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,200
Siprai!

178
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:43,240
Siprai.

179
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,040
-Siprai!
-Siprai!

180
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:50,080
-Get off me!
-Siprai!

181
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:52,440
-Stop! Siprai!
-I said stop!

182
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:55,120
Going in now won't change anything!

183
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:00,560
-Siprai!
-Siprai!

184
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:32,200
Rena… Where's Rena?

185
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,000
Rena.

186
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:04,360
I couldn't protect you…

187
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:08,960
or our parents at all.

188
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:23,840
Siprai,

189
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,440
we have to go now.

190
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:28,160
I promise,

191
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:32,360
I will avenge you,

192
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:36,280
our father and mother.

193
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:40,960
Everything they did to us,
I will do to them.

194
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:58,680
Eat up.

195
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:05,760
I'm good. You eat.

196
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:09,840
Come on. Take a bite.
My mom made this for us.

197
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,040
Siprai.

198
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:32,480
I've made up my mind. I'm leaving.

199
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,120
Leaving? Where will you go?

200
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:40,160
I'm going to join the Union Army.

201
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,080
Join them? How?

202
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:47,600
Tomorrow, we head to Naka Village.

203
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:50,960
The best Kase warriors are there.

204
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:57,280
If we can join them,
we'll become part of the Union Army.

205
00:21:58,560 --> 00:21:59,880
Count me in.

206
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:04,520
The Savins forced our hand.

207
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,200
I will kill every single one of them.

208
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:11,240
I hear you, Siprai.

209
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:14,080
No matter what happens,

210
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:18,040
we must protect our land and our people

211
00:22:18,840 --> 00:22:21,240
at all costs.

212
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:32,400
Mongjunai.

213
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,440
Did those Savins butcher
everyone down to this handful?

214
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:37,920
I'm not entirely sure,

215
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:41,080
but I think the others escaped
to hide somewhere else.

216
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:43,400
It's not safe here either.

217
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:46,960
True. There's only one place
I know for certain

218
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:50,840
where no Savin bastards
will ever harm a single Kase again.

219
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:53,120
That place is held by a brave warrior

220
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:55,600
who has never fallen to the Savins.

221
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:01,880
Colonel Layee of Naka Village.

222
00:23:05,760 --> 00:23:09,040
<i>Layee leads from the front</i>
<i>against the Savins.</i>

223
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:12,520
<i>He's as fierce as he is brave.</i>

224
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:17,240
<i>He made us believe that</i>
<i>as long as we fight,</i>

225
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:20,640
<i>the Savin government will never tear</i>

226
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:22,960
<i>our beloved homeland from us.</i>

227
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:48,920
<i>Layee showed the Savins</i>

228
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:52,120
<i>that anyone who trespasses</i>

229
00:23:52,760 --> 00:23:57,480
<i>to slaughter, harm,</i>
<i>and steal the land of the Kases</i>

230
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:59,760
<i>must die.</i>

231
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:43,680
Careful…

232
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:53,720
-Careful.
-Wait.

233
00:24:57,880 --> 00:24:59,160
Mom.

234
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:07,360
Come on.

235
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:17,120
These people are like leeches
hiding out on Thai soil.

236
00:25:22,800 --> 00:25:24,560
They secretly bleed us dry,

237
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,760
leaving our own people weak and sick.

238
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:30,520
We won't let them

239
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:34,600
use our land to make a living ever again.

240
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:01,240
Hey.

241
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:09,800
Hey, get the money bag.

242
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,000
Why the hell did you come back?

243
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:33,040
Get your hands up!

244
00:26:36,320 --> 00:26:39,520
You think you can take me?
We all die here. Out of my way!

245
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,800
-What do we do?
-Do what he says.

246
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:55,720
You bunch of fools!

247
00:26:55,800 --> 00:26:57,680
-What the--
-Get down!

248
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:12,240
You bastard!

249
00:27:43,080 --> 00:27:45,400
What kind of hell did you crawl out of?

250
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:47,200
You even kill your own people.

251
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:49,920
What's it gonna be, you scum?

252
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:52,520
You wanna die right here?
Come take a swing at me.

253
00:28:05,360 --> 00:28:06,480
Chart!

254
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:11,120
Radio for a medevac now!

255
00:28:11,960 --> 00:28:14,040
Eagle to Helipad, over.

256
00:28:14,120 --> 00:28:17,120
Eagle here, over.
Inbound for casualty extraction.

257
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:25,200
Sa.

258
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,240
Sa!

259
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:42,040
What's up with you, Yoon?
Why are you freaking out?

260
00:28:42,120 --> 00:28:43,960
Done filling it out yet?

261
00:28:44,040 --> 00:28:45,520
None of your business.

262
00:28:45,600 --> 00:28:46,640
Hmm.

263
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:49,360
-Let me see!
-Give it back!

264
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:51,560
Hey! You girls!

265
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:54,680
You put Business Admin
for all your choices?

266
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:56,600
Why, Sa?

267
00:28:57,240 --> 00:29:00,800
Honestly, I don't even want Business.

268
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:04,040
I'd much rather go into
Education or Teaching.

269
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:07,720
Right? Haven't you wanted
to be a teacher forever?

270
00:29:08,320 --> 00:29:11,320
Yeah, but my dad would never let me.

271
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:14,920
And if I fail the entrance exams,
he'll ship me off abroad

272
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:17,160
and I won't get to see you two anymore.

273
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:19,760
-No way!
-Not happening.

274
00:29:19,840 --> 00:29:21,800
You've gotta pass the exam!
Hit the books now!

275
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,680
Sa!

276
00:29:24,280 --> 00:29:26,400
-Sa, dear!
-Yes, Mom?

277
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:28,600
-Cholachart was shot.
-Huh?!

278
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:31,240
Is he alright? How bad is it?

279
00:29:31,320 --> 00:29:33,880
They said he's in emergency surgery.

280
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:35,880
Sa, please go check on him
as soon as you can!

281
00:29:36,600 --> 00:29:37,960
Yes, Mom.

282
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:44,400
Sir.

283
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:48,000
PATIENT TRANSPORT

284
00:29:48,080 --> 00:29:49,360
How is he, Doctor?

285
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:53,440
The surgery went smoothly.
Now we just have to wait for him to wake.

286
00:29:58,880 --> 00:29:59,800
Thank you, Doctor.

287
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:02,320
OPERATING ROOM

288
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:37,600
Stay still, please. Don't move just yet.

289
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,280
How did I end up here?

290
00:30:41,560 --> 00:30:45,600
What a question. If nothing was wrong,
you wouldn't be lounging here.

291
00:30:45,680 --> 00:30:46,840
You were shot.

292
00:30:47,520 --> 00:30:48,520
Oh, right.

293
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:51,280
If you need anything,
just press the call button.

294
00:30:51,800 --> 00:30:52,680
Please wait.

295
00:30:55,480 --> 00:30:56,360
Is something wrong?

296
00:30:57,600 --> 00:30:59,080
Could I ask you for a favor?

297
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:01,840
Yes.

298
00:31:01,920 --> 00:31:04,800
Please don't tell my mother yet
that I was shot

299
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:06,280
and am recovering here.

300
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:08,240
Why not?

301
00:31:08,320 --> 00:31:09,880
I don't want her to worry.

302
00:31:11,360 --> 00:31:12,280
My mother is…

303
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:14,400
Chart! Chart!

304
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:17,280
-Chart, how are you, my boy?
-Mom.

305
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:22,680
Where does it hurt, Son?
Where were you shot? Let me see the wound.

306
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:28,000
In the groin, Mom. You can't look.

307
00:31:28,080 --> 00:31:30,640
Stop joking around.

308
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:33,040
I was so worried about you.

309
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:36,200
My little baby.

310
00:31:39,120 --> 00:31:40,960
Please tell me it isn't bad.

311
00:31:43,680 --> 00:31:45,800
-Are you in a lot of pain?
-Mom.

312
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:49,560
Don't worry about me. I'm fine now.

313
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:53,280
How can you say you're fine?

314
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:58,160
You're my only child.
If something happens to you,

315
00:31:58,240 --> 00:31:59,960
who am I supposed to live for?

316
00:32:01,760 --> 00:32:02,720
Mom.

317
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,640
-Mom.
-Hm?

318
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:13,640
I can manage on my own, really.
You're so busy. No need to stay.

319
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:15,360
Don't you really know?

320
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:18,920
No job is more important than you.

321
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:22,760
I'm staying right here
until my little boy is all better.

322
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:24,400
My little boy…

323
00:32:24,480 --> 00:32:25,360
Chet.

324
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:30,800
Huh? Don't you want me here, dear?

325
00:32:30,880 --> 00:32:32,520
No, Mom. It's not that.

326
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:36,840
Then there's no problem, right?

327
00:32:37,520 --> 00:32:38,360
Yes.

328
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:48,280
Excuse me. I need
to clean the wound now, please.

329
00:32:54,120 --> 00:32:55,320
Of course. Go ahead.

330
00:32:57,240 --> 00:32:59,120
Please wait outside for a moment.

331
00:33:01,200 --> 00:33:02,040
Okay.

332
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:05,240
I'll be right back.

333
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:15,520
You literally saved me by the bell.

334
00:33:17,440 --> 00:33:19,320
I was just doing my job.

335
00:33:40,720 --> 00:33:42,200
This might sting a little.

336
00:33:51,080 --> 00:33:52,600
Your hands are so soft.

337
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:57,560
I mean you have such a gentle touch.

338
00:34:02,760 --> 00:34:05,640
Looks like I might have
to stay here for a while.

339
00:34:08,560 --> 00:34:10,280
Irene.

340
00:34:13,159 --> 00:34:14,600
Our names rhyme so perfectly.

341
00:34:15,199 --> 00:34:16,280
Cholachart?

342
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:17,440
That's right.

343
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:19,880
It's my English name.

344
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:24,000
You're Irene and I'm…

345
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:35,040
Chart!

346
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:45,639
Oh, did I hurt you?

347
00:34:46,239 --> 00:34:48,360
Sorry. You're all set now.

348
00:35:02,760 --> 00:35:04,240
How is it going?

349
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:08,720
I'm totally fine.
Just relaxing here for a bit.

350
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,040
Pretty, isn't she?

351
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:18,480
That nurse.

352
00:35:38,640 --> 00:35:40,320
What's wrong with you, Irene?

353
00:35:40,400 --> 00:35:44,720
Nate, why do guys love to flirt so much?

354
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:47,720
Acting like they're into us
when they already have girlfriends.

355
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:52,280
That handsome soldier?

356
00:35:53,960 --> 00:35:57,440
Right? Spill it.

357
00:35:59,320 --> 00:36:00,360
I don't know.

358
00:36:01,200 --> 00:36:03,840
How long do you need
to stay in the hospital, Chart?

359
00:36:04,840 --> 00:36:07,600
Not sure yet. But don't worry, Sa.

360
00:36:07,680 --> 00:36:09,640
I can take care of myself, easy-peasy.

361
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:14,920
Take care of yourself? Or do you just
want someone else to take care of you?

362
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:16,080
Who?

363
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:18,920
That pretty nurse!

364
00:36:22,120 --> 00:36:24,720
Be honest, do you like her?

365
00:36:26,640 --> 00:36:28,800
-Nope!
-Nope?

366
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:32,320
COMMISSIONED OFFICERS ROOM

367
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:33,240
Stop!

368
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:38,680
-Your voice went way up!
-Nope.

369
00:36:48,040 --> 00:36:48,920
Look at you.

370
00:36:50,440 --> 00:36:51,400
I'm totally serious!

371
00:36:52,320 --> 00:36:54,600
Oh, is that so?

372
00:36:54,680 --> 00:36:56,600
Then do you wanna know

373
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:59,440
if that pretty nurse is single?

374
00:36:59,520 --> 00:37:01,400
-Yes!
-There it is.

375
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:02,840
I knew it!

376
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:16,760
Yiaza.

377
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:19,680
We got new refugees coming in.

378
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:22,560
Take him home.

379
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:51,720
Get the elders taken care of first.

380
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:54,480
Welcome, everyone.

381
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:57,080
We live here as family.

382
00:37:57,720 --> 00:37:59,920
Whatever food we have, we share.

383
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:01,880
When enemies come,

384
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:04,760
we fight together.

385
00:38:06,080 --> 00:38:10,120
As Kase brethren, no matter where we are,

386
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:12,640
we stand united.

387
00:38:22,080 --> 00:38:23,920
-Mom! Mom!
-Auntie Mawae.

388
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:26,360
-Are you okay?
-Make way!

389
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:29,040
Get her to the infirmary.

390
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:31,920
Mom.

391
00:38:36,920 --> 00:38:38,360
Aunt Mawae has low blood pressure

392
00:38:38,440 --> 00:38:40,640
and travel fatigue.

393
00:38:40,720 --> 00:38:44,520
Rest and medicine are
all she needs. She'll be fine.

394
00:38:44,600 --> 00:38:47,080
Does my mother
need to stay overnight at the infirmary?

395
00:38:48,040 --> 00:38:51,080
No need. Once she wakes up,
she can rest at the quarters.

396
00:38:53,960 --> 00:38:55,640
Thank you very much.

397
00:38:57,200 --> 00:38:58,280
I'm Manu.

398
00:38:58,360 --> 00:39:01,920
I'm the head medic here.
Let me know if you need anything.

399
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:04,080
I’ll do whatever I can to help.

400
00:39:05,280 --> 00:39:10,560
I'm Mintada. I came here
to join the Kases warriors

401
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:12,040
to fight those Savin bastards.

402
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:15,880
I'm glad to have
a brave man like you in the fight.

403
00:39:21,280 --> 00:39:24,080
Siprai. Look at that nurse!

404
00:39:24,160 --> 00:39:26,760
Why is she making eyes at my Mintada?

405
00:39:31,720 --> 00:39:34,200
Siprai. Are you listening to me?

406
00:39:34,720 --> 00:39:35,920
So beautiful.

407
00:39:36,520 --> 00:39:37,440
I don't see it.

408
00:39:38,040 --> 00:39:39,360
Look at her.

409
00:39:40,120 --> 00:39:41,280
Pale skin.

410
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:44,640
Big bug eyes, nose way too sharp.

411
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:46,480
Can't compare to me, right?

412
00:39:47,600 --> 00:39:48,520
Yeah, true.

413
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:50,880
She can't compare to you.

414
00:39:52,160 --> 00:39:54,040
Well, don't exaggerate.

415
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:08,120
Wow!

416
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:09,680
That's so cool.

417
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:14,320
If I had a gun,
I'd wipe out every last Savin.

418
00:40:15,320 --> 00:40:19,440
It won't be long, Siprai.
Soon we'll join the troops

419
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:22,160
and wear the uniform of Kase warriors.

420
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:26,400
Fight side by side with
a hero like Colonel Layee.

421
00:40:26,480 --> 00:40:28,320
I pray that day comes soon.

422
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:30,240
Me too.

423
00:40:31,080 --> 00:40:31,920
Same here.

424
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:34,560
Not you. You're just a girl.

425
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:38,800
Why can't a woman be a warrior?
You know nothing, so shut your mouth.

426
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:43,880
Did you know Naka Village has women
warriors? Yiaza is the head of the unit.

427
00:40:43,960 --> 00:40:47,160
You should join the medics instead.

428
00:40:47,240 --> 00:40:49,200
Manu said they're short-handed.

429
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:50,320
Ugh.

430
00:40:50,400 --> 00:40:52,360
Come on, as if Khengla
could look after anyone!

431
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:56,200
Unlike Manu,
she's beautiful, cute, talented,

432
00:40:56,280 --> 00:40:58,040
gentle, and so sweet--

433
00:40:58,120 --> 00:40:59,520
Shut it! That's enough!

434
00:41:00,640 --> 00:41:02,720
If Manu can do it, so can I.

435
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:04,960
And I'll do it better. Just you watch.

436
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:18,600
Manu, are you betrothed already?

437
00:41:19,200 --> 00:41:21,120
My hands are full with work.

438
00:41:22,200 --> 00:41:23,960
I have no time for a betrothed.

439
00:41:26,880 --> 00:41:27,880
Manu.

440
00:41:30,520 --> 00:41:32,280
I brought you some bamboo shoots.

441
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:33,680
Thanks, Yapo.

442
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:37,720
I'll ask the cooks
to boil them and share with everyone.

443
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:40,640
Okay. So I'll…

444
00:41:41,760 --> 00:41:43,520
I'll just leave them right here then.

445
00:41:43,600 --> 00:41:44,880
Okay.

446
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:46,000
Okay.

447
00:41:52,240 --> 00:41:54,840
Thought you said
you didn't have a betrothed.

448
00:41:55,560 --> 00:41:57,400
-That's not it!
-Yeah?

449
00:41:58,640 --> 00:42:00,080
Why are you teasing me?

450
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:06,400
Don't be shy.

451
00:42:07,640 --> 00:42:08,720
Zip it!

452
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:14,080
Mintada, I think I like Manu.

453
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:15,600
Siprai!

454
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:18,200
You're so easy.
You fall for everyone you see.

455
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:22,880
Nah. I had a crush on her back in the day.

456
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:25,120
I used to steal glances all the time.

457
00:42:25,200 --> 00:42:27,840
She's as gorgeous as an angel.

458
00:42:27,920 --> 00:42:29,480
Man, you are down bad.

459
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:31,200
Mintada.

460
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:34,920
Do you think it's possible

461
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:36,960
for Mama Mawae to propose to Manu for me?

462
00:42:37,560 --> 00:42:39,640
Isn't that a bit too soon?

463
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:43,800
Not right now! I mean in the future.

464
00:42:43,880 --> 00:42:44,720
Hey!

465
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:48,600
What did you just say?

466
00:42:48,680 --> 00:42:52,320
Say what?
Whatever I said is none of your business.

467
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:55,280
It is my business,
because the Manu you mentioned

468
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:57,680
is my betrothed.

469
00:42:58,840 --> 00:43:00,640
-Your betrothed?
-Yes.

470
00:43:00,720 --> 00:43:03,840
As far as I know,
Manu never cared about you.

471
00:43:04,520 --> 00:43:05,480
Siprai!

472
00:43:08,760 --> 00:43:10,120
Siprai, no!

473
00:43:12,720 --> 00:43:16,120
Weird. The rains are here

474
00:43:16,200 --> 00:43:18,840
but the Savins
still keep bombing Kase villages.

475
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:23,720
They must've changed tactics.

476
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:27,440
But I'm not afraid.

477
00:43:29,680 --> 00:43:31,960
Colonel! Colonel!

478
00:43:32,040 --> 00:43:33,200
What's all the racket?

479
00:43:33,280 --> 00:43:34,520
There's trouble, Colonel.

480
00:43:37,240 --> 00:43:38,440
Siprai, Stop!

481
00:43:48,280 --> 00:43:49,280
Snap out of it!

482
00:43:51,200 --> 00:43:52,400
Why are you fighting each other?!

483
00:43:52,480 --> 00:43:55,360
The Savins are our enemy, not the Kases!

484
00:43:55,440 --> 00:43:58,080
It's him. He disrespected Manu.

485
00:43:59,000 --> 00:44:00,120
She’s my girl.

486
00:44:00,200 --> 00:44:02,120
I was never yours.

487
00:44:02,200 --> 00:44:06,120
Then what about the woven cloth
you gave me? What did that mean?

488
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:08,840
That was for a friend, not a lover.

489
00:44:09,520 --> 00:44:12,720
Get it straight.
Friendship is all I can give you.

490
00:44:15,160 --> 00:44:17,320
This is the final warning.

491
00:44:18,360 --> 00:44:21,200
From now on, if anyone fights again,

492
00:44:22,760 --> 00:44:25,040
I'll banish you all from Naka

493
00:44:25,640 --> 00:44:27,040
whether you're old

494
00:44:29,120 --> 00:44:30,160
or new.

495
00:44:33,640 --> 00:44:34,720
Shake hands now.

496
00:44:37,960 --> 00:44:39,400
Shake on it man.

497
00:44:39,480 --> 00:44:41,160
Shake hands now!

498
00:44:49,880 --> 00:44:52,760
From now on, you two are friends.

499
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:55,040
-Friends?
-Hey!

500
00:44:55,120 --> 00:44:56,240
Yes.

501
00:44:57,760 --> 00:44:59,200
Go to the training field tomorrow.

502
00:45:00,080 --> 00:45:02,640
Let's see if you can do
more than just throw punches.

503
00:45:04,480 --> 00:45:05,800
You too.

504
00:45:06,800 --> 00:45:09,360
Be at the training ground
at dawn. Understood?

505
00:45:11,040 --> 00:45:13,160
Does this mean Siprai and I

506
00:45:13,240 --> 00:45:15,320
get to join the Kase warriors now?

507
00:45:15,400 --> 00:45:17,480
We are the Kases.

508
00:45:18,600 --> 00:45:20,320
We must stand as one.

509
00:45:21,400 --> 00:45:23,880
Nothing will tear us apart.

510
00:45:24,760 --> 00:45:26,040
We don't fight each other.

511
00:45:26,720 --> 00:45:30,840
We fight our enemy to the death!

512
00:45:36,560 --> 00:45:38,480
Mom. Mom.

513
00:45:40,880 --> 00:45:43,080
What are you so happy about, Mintada?

514
00:45:43,160 --> 00:45:45,840
I'm finally joining the Kase warriors.

515
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:47,720
And soon,

516
00:45:47,800 --> 00:45:50,680
I'll be a Union soldier.

517
00:46:03,880 --> 00:46:06,600
I can't bear to lose another child.

518
00:46:14,080 --> 00:46:15,320
Dad. It's the Savin bastards.

519
00:46:16,200 --> 00:46:17,440
Methawin, get down!

520
00:46:17,960 --> 00:46:20,280
-Santha.
-Mawae. Mintada. Hide!

521
00:46:21,040 --> 00:46:21,880
Quick! Quick!

522
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:25,480
Savin bastards!

523
00:46:25,560 --> 00:46:27,920
Bring thousands or tens of thousands.

524
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:30,120
I won't back down an inch!

525
00:46:30,200 --> 00:46:31,800
Remember this!

526
00:46:31,880 --> 00:46:34,200
This land is mine.

527
00:46:34,280 --> 00:46:36,440
It belongs to every Kase!

528
00:46:38,640 --> 00:46:40,680
Methawin. Go! Go!

529
00:46:53,680 --> 00:46:55,080
Mom.

530
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:58,000
If dad and Methawin were still here,

531
00:46:58,080 --> 00:46:59,840
they'd do the same.

532
00:47:03,560 --> 00:47:04,760
Dad!

533
00:47:09,640 --> 00:47:11,960
They would fight just like me…

534
00:47:14,960 --> 00:47:16,600
and every Kase soldier.

535
00:47:19,320 --> 00:47:21,680
What is the meaning of our lives

536
00:47:22,360 --> 00:47:24,880
if not to protect this land

537
00:47:25,600 --> 00:47:27,080
for those we love?

538
00:48:00,880 --> 00:48:03,960
Everyone must stay alive
to reclaim the nation of Kase!

539
00:48:04,560 --> 00:48:08,200
Everyone must stay alive
to reclaim the nation of Kase!

540
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:14,040
Kase warriors never die!

541
00:48:14,120 --> 00:48:16,480
Kase warriors never die!

542
00:48:19,560 --> 00:48:22,720
Everyone must stay alive
to reclaim the nation of Kase!

543
00:48:23,320 --> 00:48:24,800
-Everyone must stay alive…
-Everyone must stay alive

544
00:48:24,880 --> 00:48:27,240
to reclaim the nation of Kase!

545
00:48:28,760 --> 00:48:30,280
Stay alive…

546
00:48:31,760 --> 00:48:33,720
to reclaim the nation of Kase!

547
00:48:35,720 --> 00:48:37,440
-Mintada.
-Mintada.

548
00:48:39,720 --> 00:48:41,360
Mintada…

549
00:49:04,480 --> 00:49:07,640
Everyone must stay alive
to reclaim the nation of Kase!

550
00:49:08,720 --> 00:49:10,400
Everyone must stay alive…

551
00:49:11,040 --> 00:49:13,600
To reclaim the nation of Kase!

552
00:49:20,880 --> 00:49:23,160
Kase warriors never die!

553
00:49:23,240 --> 00:49:25,120
Kase warriors

554
00:49:26,080 --> 00:49:27,400
-never die!
-Never die!

555
00:49:30,880 --> 00:49:31,800
Mintada!

556
00:49:31,880 --> 00:49:33,480
-Mintada.
-Mintada.

557
00:49:51,960 --> 00:49:55,280
Halt the punishment. Take him away.

558
00:49:55,360 --> 00:49:57,880
Mintada, Son. Mintada.

559
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:00,440
Let's go.

560
00:50:08,040 --> 00:50:09,800
Kase warriors never die.

561
00:50:11,680 --> 00:50:13,480
Never die.

562
00:50:25,880 --> 00:50:27,600
How are you holding up, Mintada?

563
00:50:28,600 --> 00:50:30,640
I've stitched up your wound.

564
00:50:31,240 --> 00:50:32,720
Luckily, the bullet wasn't inside.

565
00:50:33,720 --> 00:50:35,680
Get plenty of rest, Mintada.

566
00:50:36,680 --> 00:50:38,240
Thank you very much, Manu.

567
00:50:38,920 --> 00:50:40,360
It's my duty.

568
00:51:09,600 --> 00:51:12,400
So annoying! If Mintada weren't here,

569
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:14,440
she'd get a taste of my slap!

570
00:51:14,520 --> 00:51:16,840
Stop right there! If you touch Manu,

571
00:51:16,920 --> 00:51:19,760
I'll make you suffer
a thousand times worse.

572
00:51:24,440 --> 00:51:25,720
What is wrong with everyone?!

573
00:51:25,800 --> 00:51:27,720
Why does everyone only care about Manu?

574
00:51:27,800 --> 00:51:30,640
What about me?
What about this girl Khengla?

575
00:51:35,000 --> 00:51:36,160
This isn't over yet.

576
00:51:52,720 --> 00:51:56,480
Mom. Why are you crying?

577
00:51:58,560 --> 00:52:00,400
I'm alright now.

578
00:52:17,800 --> 00:52:19,880
So you're really not studying abroad, Sa?

579
00:52:19,960 --> 00:52:22,760
No, I'm not.
I want to study here in Thailand.

580
00:52:23,280 --> 00:52:25,440
Look, I even chose the faculty

581
00:52:25,960 --> 00:52:27,920
dad wanted me to get into.

582
00:52:28,760 --> 00:52:31,280
But I really wish I could study Education.

583
00:52:32,480 --> 00:52:35,080
Ah, right. You've always
wanted to be a teacher.

584
00:52:36,400 --> 00:52:39,880
But whatever. It doesn't matter
what you study. I just ask for one thing.

585
00:52:40,640 --> 00:52:42,520
As long as you're close to me,
that's enough.

586
00:52:43,520 --> 00:52:46,200
Without you, I'd be so lonely.

587
00:52:46,280 --> 00:52:48,080
Oh, wow!

588
00:52:48,160 --> 00:52:51,160
A workaholic like you
actually has time to be lonely?

589
00:52:51,840 --> 00:52:53,280
Sometimes I do.

590
00:52:56,480 --> 00:52:57,960
Do you want to cure loneliness?

591
00:52:58,040 --> 00:52:59,720
Is that even a question? Absolutely.

592
00:53:00,400 --> 00:53:01,880
Then let me help you.

593
00:53:02,960 --> 00:53:07,000
Sa! Where are you going?
You brought me here, now take me back!

594
00:53:08,920 --> 00:53:10,160
What on earth?

595
00:53:12,040 --> 00:53:13,480
Now how am I supposed to get back?

596
00:53:27,440 --> 00:53:28,360
Got dumped?

597
00:53:29,960 --> 00:53:33,920
That's the trouble with younger lovers.
Teens have mood swings all the time.

598
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:35,640
You'd better learn to live with it.

599
00:53:37,080 --> 00:53:38,160
You've got it all wrong.

600
00:53:38,240 --> 00:53:39,680
What did I get wrong?

601
00:53:40,440 --> 00:53:42,000
Sa is my sister.

602
00:53:43,640 --> 00:53:45,520
You're a terrible liar.

603
00:53:46,880 --> 00:53:48,120
I'm not lying.

604
00:53:49,760 --> 00:53:52,400
The other day, your mom clearly
said you were an only child.

605
00:53:54,280 --> 00:53:55,160
That's true.

606
00:53:56,400 --> 00:53:57,800
She's not my biological sister,

607
00:53:58,400 --> 00:54:01,480
but we grew up together.
It's no different.

608
00:54:07,440 --> 00:54:10,320
Whatever. Believe what you want.

609
00:54:11,480 --> 00:54:14,280
At least I hope that as a nurse,

610
00:54:14,800 --> 00:54:17,960
you'll have some mercy
on poor helpless patients.

611
00:54:20,840 --> 00:54:24,640
Of course.
Strictly as a nurse to a patient.

612
00:54:31,280 --> 00:54:34,200
Irene, not only are you beautiful,
but you're kindhearted too.

613
00:54:46,560 --> 00:54:48,480
Now those Savin bastards feel invincible

614
00:54:49,000 --> 00:54:51,600
after torching so many of our homes.

615
00:54:52,920 --> 00:54:55,240
Their overconfidence is our opening.

616
00:54:55,840 --> 00:54:58,120
This is our chance to strike back.

617
00:55:02,120 --> 00:55:03,720
What's your plan?

618
00:55:03,800 --> 00:55:06,080
We'll lure them into a trap

619
00:55:06,160 --> 00:55:09,600
on our own turf, then finish them off.

620
00:55:10,640 --> 00:55:11,520
Where?

621
00:55:13,720 --> 00:55:15,360
The Cursed Forest to the west.

622
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:20,440
We'll divide the Kase warriors
into three units.

623
00:55:21,640 --> 00:55:24,760
The first will lure the Savins
into the Cursed Forest.

624
00:55:26,520 --> 00:55:30,760
The other two units will ambush
from the north and south.

625
00:55:32,040 --> 00:55:33,760
Once they're inside,

626
00:55:33,840 --> 00:55:35,520
rain down hell.

627
00:55:36,080 --> 00:55:38,880
No one leaves the Cursed Forest alive.

628
00:55:38,960 --> 00:55:40,880
But if we do that,

629
00:55:41,400 --> 00:55:43,560
I fear we won't have enough warriors.

630
00:55:43,640 --> 00:55:48,280
We must use everyone we've got, including
the new recruits who just joined us.

631
00:55:49,080 --> 00:55:51,200
Colonel, are you sure about this?

632
00:55:51,280 --> 00:55:52,960
They've barely started training.

633
00:55:54,360 --> 00:55:57,840
The battlefield
is the best training ground.

634
00:56:07,080 --> 00:56:08,520
If our men aren't enough,

635
00:56:10,720 --> 00:56:13,760
my women's unit is ready
to ride into battle with you.

636
00:56:15,760 --> 00:56:16,720
Yiaza.

637
00:56:17,400 --> 00:56:20,640
It's none of your business.
Let the men talk.

638
00:56:21,800 --> 00:56:23,600
I'll call you if we need you.

639
00:56:23,680 --> 00:56:27,960
Why? Man or woman,
the same Kase blood runs through us all.

640
00:56:28,040 --> 00:56:32,200
My women's unit stands ready
to fight shoulder to shoulder with you.

641
00:56:35,040 --> 00:56:35,880
Yiaza.

642
00:56:37,120 --> 00:56:38,520
I appreciate it.

643
00:56:39,960 --> 00:56:41,480
But as my father said,

644
00:56:42,880 --> 00:56:45,800
if we need anything, we'll let you know.

645
00:56:51,360 --> 00:56:53,000
We'll use the new recruits as bait.

646
00:56:53,080 --> 00:56:55,160
They don't need to do much.

647
00:56:55,240 --> 00:56:57,600
They just need to survive

648
00:56:58,280 --> 00:57:01,080
until Savin's troops
walk right into the Cursed Forest.

649
00:57:02,240 --> 00:57:03,400
What do you think?

650
00:57:25,840 --> 00:57:30,160
<i>Upon the highest land</i>
<i>God has called us to…</i>

651
00:57:30,240 --> 00:57:31,680
Come back safe.

652
00:57:31,760 --> 00:57:34,160
<i>…lies a life of beauty and abundance</i>

653
00:57:47,840 --> 00:57:49,640
What did we do wrong to be punished?

654
00:57:49,720 --> 00:57:51,120
Why did you ban us from battle?

655
00:57:51,200 --> 00:57:52,400
You two must go to Thailand.

656
00:57:53,000 --> 00:57:54,640
<i>I have faith in you.</i>

657
00:58:49,280 --> 00:58:51,280
Subtitle translation by: Onamon Chai
